WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:04.584
From a wedding-parent makeup specialist:

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.680
<How to be the happiest wedding parent on the day>

3
00:00:08.016 --> 00:00:11.928
Becoming a wedding parent for the first time brings excitement and fear together.

4
00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:14.160
It is only one day,

5
00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:18.864
but you are the host who invited all those guests, and many eyes are on you,

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.144
and it stays on record —

7
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.144
so it isn't a role you can take lightly.

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.256
When careful, professional care makes you happy with the face in the mirror,

9
00:00:29.592 --> 00:00:32.688
you finally set out with anticipation instead of nerves.

10
00:00:33.024 --> 00:00:37.296
Careful makeup and hair only lay the foundation of that confidence;

11
00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:40.848
what completes the day is the bright smile you add on top of it.

12
00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:44.304
That is what wedding-parent makeup is for.

13
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.416
Remember this:

14
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:48.984
<a light heart> and <a bright smile>.

15
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.544
Those two are the secret to being the happiest wedding parent at the ceremony.

16
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.712
Having met so many different wedding parents,

17
00:00:57.048 --> 00:00:59.952
and giving our best to each and every one,

18
00:01:00.288 --> 00:01:04.488
we gathered the questions you send us into these 100 questions and answers.

19
00:01:04.824 --> 00:01:07.368
We hope they genuinely help.

20
00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:11.832
And if you have any other questions of your own, please ask anytime.

21
00:01:12.168 --> 00:01:14.448
We will answer gladly.

22
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:24.600
You can reach us by email at makeupforl@naver.com, by phone at 010-8315-3323, and through our KakaoTalk channel.

23
00:01:24.936 --> 00:01:27.864
Wishing our wedding parents a beautiful day,

24
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.080
Makeup for L, director Kim Seong-hee.
